{"id": "library-branch-prevailing-wage-orders", "title": "Two corrected orders trace $101,352 in unpaid wages to two SF branch libraries", "seconds": 49.6, "voice": "elevenlabs:OUMCzFUTd0F4Q6lkLkco", "narrator": "Roxy", "tempo": 1.119, "made": "2026-11-26", "key": "c619a73fba3dda82", "words": 131, "beats": [{"scene": "projects", "kind": "hook", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "The Merced and Visitacion Valley library branches both opened in 2011.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.54, "shot": "r0", "visual": {"type": "hook", "words": ["Who", "worked", "on", "the", "two", "libraries?"], "sub": "San Francisco branch renovations"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.53, 0.63, 1.37, 1.71, 2.16, 2.64, 2.97, 3.35, 3.47, 3.88]}, {"scene": "projects", "kind": "record", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "The library records name CLW Builders. The state wage orders identify its subcontractor, Shamrock Structures.", "t0": 4.66, "t1": 11.52, "shot": "r1", "visual": {"type": "record", "layout": "relationship", "context": "The same contractors at both branches", "heading": "How the work was awarded", "source": "visitacion", "rows": [{"icon": "cityhall", "label": "Awarding body", "value": "San Francisco Public Works"}, {"icon": "contract", "label": "Prime contractor", "value": "CLW Builders"}, {"icon": "building", "label": "Subcontractor", "value": "Shamrock Structures"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.58, 0.99, 1.25, 1.94, 3.04, 3.21, 3.52, 3.83, 4.15, 4.67, 4.82, 5.67, 6.19]}, {"scene": "projects", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "The state found Shamrock used incorrect classifications and failed to pay the required compensation.", "t0": 11.64, "t1": 16.92, "shot": "r2", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "merced", "kicker": "California Department of Industrial Relations", "text": "Worker classifications", "mark": "Worker classifications"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.44, 0.7, 1.28, 1.54, 1.99, 2.97, 3.21, 3.51, 3.59, 3.8, 3.91, 4.39]}, {"scene": "orders", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "After a 2013 hearing, enforcement staff credited payroll checks and reduced the wage amounts.", "t0": 17.14, "t1": 22.39, "shot": "r3", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "visitacion", "kicker": "California Department of Industrial Relations", "text": "Payroll checks", "mark": "Payroll checks"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.32, 0.38, 0.69, 1.18, 1.66, 2.26, 2.59, 3.02, 3.41, 3.8, 3.98, 4.35, 4.46, 4.74]}, {"scene": "orders", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "The original decisions switched the libraries’ case numbers and named the wrong subcontractor.", "t0": 22.51, "t1": 27.06, "shot": "r4", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "merced", "kicker": "California Department of Industrial Relations", "text": "January 2017 corrections", "mark": "January 2017 corrections"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.53, 1.1, 1.53, 1.64, 2.15, 2.45, 2.8, 2.91, 3.1, 3.19, 3.52]}, {"scene": "orders", "kind": "record", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[2]"], "text": "Visitacion Valley accounted for the larger wage amount. Merced accounted for the rest.", "t0": 27.18, "t1": 31.72, "shot": "r5", "visual": {"type": "record", "layout": "amounts", "context": "Corrected wage awards", "heading": "Wages remaining by branch", "source": "visitacion", "rows": [{"icon": "money", "label": "Visitacion Valley", "value": "$64,142.85"}, {"icon": "money", "label": "Merced", "value": "$37,209.27"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.62, 0.92, 1.36, 1.48, 1.59, 1.94, 2.2, 2.99, 3.39, 3.83, 3.95, 4.06]}, {"scene": "orders", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[2]"], "text": "Together the wage amounts totaled $101,352.12.", "t0": 31.84, "t1": 36.93, "shot": "r6", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$101,352.12", "label": "Unpaid wages in the orders"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.41, 0.51, 0.79, 1.23, 1.67, 1.86, 2.18, 2.38, 2.82, 3.06, 3.33, 3.82, 4.21, 4.29, 4.62]}, {"scene": "orders", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[2]"], "text": "The orders also included liquidated damages, training contributions and penalties, with interest additional.", "t0": 37.05, "t1": 42.68, "shot": "r7", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Damages and penalties"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.51, 0.79, 1.18, 1.72, 2.36, 2.78, 3.52, 3.71, 4.33, 4.56, 5.0]}, {"scene": "orders", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]"], "text": "The orders do not establish how much the workers ultimately collected.", "t0": 42.8, "t1": 46.21, "shot": "r8", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Collection"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.49, 0.62, 0.79, 1.28, 1.46, 1.69, 1.8, 2.25, 2.78]}, {"scene": "orders", "kind": "end", "ref": ["status"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 46.33, "t1": 48.65, "shot": "r9", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.37, 0.72, 0.87, 1.16, 1.24, 1.32, 1.59, 1.88]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"projects": "Who did the library work?", "orders": "Read the corrected orders"}, "look": "kinetic", "hook": "question"}